@startuml lifetime_usage_flow
title Session Lifetime Usage - Atomic Persistence and Authoritative Snapshots
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java@6f52fddc87a03c20916fc7b6ef1de87f6a7a8cf5.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventProjector.java:persistAssistant,projectCompactionCompleted.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository.java:appendEntryWithUsage,accumulateUsageStats.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/mapper/session/RuntimeSessionMapper.xml:findSession,lockSessionForUpdate.
' Observed behavior: Entry, Usage Record, sequence, leaf and coarse stats already share one transaction.
' Design reason: preserve original usage parts and read stats after acquiring the authoritative session lock.
' Java divergence: this is a Java database and HTTP resource extension, not a claim about pi HTTP behavior.
skinparam shadowing false
participant "RuntimeEventProjector\nper execution" as Projector
participant "Session Repository\nstateless singleton" as Repository
database "Session + Entry + Record + Stats" as Database
participant "Existing Session services\nstateless singletons" as Service
participant "RuntimeSessionResponseAssembler\nstateless singleton" as Assembler
participant "Read-only Session VO\nper response" as Response

group Atomic usage append
  Projector -> Repository : appendEntryWithUsage(entry, record, usage)
  Repository -> Database : lock Session row
  Repository -> Database : read Stats after lock
  Repository -> Database : append Entry + Record / advance sequence + leaf
  Repository -> Database : increment original token and cost parts
  Repository -> Database : commit all or roll back all
  Repository --> Projector : persisted domain Entry
end
group Query or configuration result
  Service -> Repository : read or update Session
  alt read
    Repository -> Database : one SELECT joins Session + Stats
  else configuration transaction
    Repository -> Database : lock Session row
    Repository -> Database : read Stats after lock wait
    Repository -> Database : preserve or update configuration
  end
  Repository --> Service : one authoritative RuntimeSessionDTO
  Service -> Assembler : project same DTO
  Assembler -> Response : copy Session + long counters + decimal costs
  Assembler --> Service : response VO + existing configuration ETag
end
note over Assembler,Response
  No mutable DTO reference escapes.
  Usage append does not advance the configuration version.
  Future Slash application reuses this projection;
  no Command HTTP route is introduced in this slice.
end note
@enduml
